From ceb0b81aab7120b5fb6bf960c1b24fb1dd009cf8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Tue, 19 May 2026 14:44:29 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] perf phase 11 patch 0162-v2 -- Leg A audio mid-gap pump v2
 (486-campaign Bug 1; v1-iter response)

486-campaign Bug 1 -- the operator's "~1-second freeze" with audio
cutout when entering a stage on a DX2-66. flush-instr #75 root-caused
it as gap-driven: during a stage load the main thread is blocked in
fread (tileset, map, entities, script), the SB16 IRQ-5 ISR keeps
draining the audio ring at ~43 Hz throughout, and the cooperative
audio thread cannot refill -- it runs only when the main thread
yields, which fread does not do. A stage load longer than the ring
depth (~372 ms) underruns the ring and audio cuts out.

v1 (the prior cut of this patch) inserted six MIDGAP_PUMP() calls in
load_stage between sub-loaders to top up the ring on otherwise-idle
CPU. The v1 iter (per 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS sec.17) showed two
regressions: (a) freeze elimination failed -- v1's once-per-seam pump
did not eliminate the >500 ms Mimiga curmap=1005 entry spike; (b) TAS
desync -- PLAY1 (pumps active) missed Shack while PLAY0 (killswitch=0,
no pumps) reached all 5 stages, because the pumps' wall-clock cost
during stage loads cascaded through the FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator:
now_ns - last_ns grew, accum_ns gained extra ticks, and the catch-up
loop ran more tick_state ticks than the TAS recording expected.

v2 ships three changes, combined into a single amended 0162:

FIX 1 -- pump until ring-full. The MIDGAP_PUMP macro wraps the pump
in `while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { }`. SDL_DOSAudioPump (SDL/0067-v2's
amended bool-return ABI) returns true while there is room for another
chunk and false when the ring is full or no-op. Each seam now tops up
to FULL instead of one chunk. Addresses v1's regression (a).

FIX 2 -- FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator freeze/thaw across load_stage.
Promotes the run_tick_fixed function-local statics accum_ns, last_ns,
ft_inited to file-scope in main.cpp (collision-clean per grep -- those
identifiers are referenced only inside run_tick_fixed; no other src/
TU uses them); adds ft_accumulator_freeze() and ft_accumulator_thaw()
helpers at file scope (freeze records accum_ns to a snapshot slot;
thaw restores accum_ns and resets last_ns to SDL_GetTicksNS() so the
load wall-clock is invisible to the next delta). map.cpp's load_stage
declares an FtAccumulatorGuard RAII struct at function entry; its
destructor fires on every return path (5 error early-returns + 1
success-path final return), so the accumulator is never left frozen.
Both freeze and thaw are gated on midgap_pump_active() -- when the
killswitch is off (the v2 default; see FIX 3), the guard is a no-op
pair and the FT=1 path is byte-identical to v1.0.0 / pre-Leg-A
(matches the v1 iter's PLAY0-clean baseline per 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-
FINDINGS sec.17 asymmetry). Addresses v1's regression (b).

FIX 3 -- killswitch default flip ON -> OFF. The killswitch parse
becomes (e[0]=='1')?1:0 (opt-in form; was (e[0]=='0')?0:1). Banner
text flips to "ENABLED (opt-in)" / "DISABLED (default)". Per flush-
instr's safer-landing recommendation: the lever ships opt-in until
the v2 iter validates that FIX 1 + FIX 2 eliminate both regressions;
v3 will promote back to default-ON if so. While default-OFF, the
FT=1 default path runs the v1.0.0 behavior exactly (no pumps, no
freeze/thaw) -- preserving the operator's TAS-replay baseline.

The 6 MIDGAP_PUMP() insertion sites in load_stage (line 970, after-
971, after-980, after-984, after-988, after-992) are unchanged from
v1; the macro semantics are what changed (FIX 1). The FtAccumulatorGuard
is added once at the top of load_stage.

SDL_DOSAudioPump's safety properties (no SDL renderer touch, no
SDL_PumpEvents, no engine-callback re-entry beyond Pixtone's scalar
slot bookkeeping) are unchanged. load_stage runs once per stage entry
(no multi-run amplification, no wave-36 trap risk).

Two-file edit: vendor/nxengine-evo/src/main.cpp (file-scope promotion
of accum_ns / last_ns / ft_inited + ft_accumulator_freeze/thaw
helpers) and vendor/nxengine-evo/src/map.cpp (the v2 helper-block
rewrite + MIDGAP_PUMP macro change + FtAccumulatorGuard RAII struct +
the FtAccumulatorGuard declaration at load_stage entry).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.7 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/main.cpp |  38 ++++++++++++++++++--
 src/map.cpp  | 100 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 135 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/main.cpp b/src/main.cpp
index e968fbf..1e77ee0 100644
--- a/src/main.cpp
+++ b/src/main.cpp
@@ -284,12 +284,44 @@ static inline void run_tick()
 // function replicates run_tick()'s essential per-frame machinery
 // (update_fps / the flipacceltime flip path / runFade / heartbeat /
 // TAS auto-exit) rather than refactoring run_tick().
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0162-v2, Leg A FIX 2 -- FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator
+// snapshot/restore across load_stage). The three state variables that
+// were function-local statics inside run_tick_fixed (accum_ns, last_ns,
+// ft_inited) are promoted to file scope here so nxengine-evo/0162-v2's
+// load_stage RAII guard can snapshot/restore them around the stage load.
+// Without the freeze/thaw, the Leg A pumps' wall-clock cost during
+// stage loads cascades through the accumulator: now_ns - last_ns grows,
+// accum_ns gains extra ticks, and the catch-up loop runs more
+// tick_state ticks than the TAS recording expected -- the v1 iter's
+// PLAY1 symptom (missed Shack while PLAY0 reached all 5 stages). See
+// docs/internal/486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.17. The promotion is
+// collision-clean (verified: only run_tick_fixed references these
+// identifiers; no other src/ TU does).
+static Uint64 accum_ns  = 0;
+static Uint64 last_ns   = 0;
+static bool   ft_inited = false;
+
+// Snapshot slot for ft_accumulator_freeze() / ft_accumulator_thaw().
+// load_stage is non-reentrant so a single slot suffices.
+static Uint64 s_ft_accum_saved = 0;
+
+// Engine hooks for nxengine-evo/0162-v2's load_stage freeze/thaw. The
+// caller (map.cpp's FtAccumulatorGuard RAII struct) gates both on
+// midgap_pump_active() -- when the Leg A killswitch is off (the v2
+// default), neither fires and the FT=1 path matches v1.0.0 / pre-Leg-A.
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_freeze(void)
+{
+  s_ft_accum_saved = accum_ns;
+}
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_thaw(void)
+{
+  accum_ns = s_ft_accum_saved;
+  last_ns  = SDL_GetTicksNS();  // exclude load_stage wall-clock from the next delta
+}
+
 static void run_tick_fixed(void)
 {
   static int frameskip      = 0;
-  static Uint64 accum_ns    = 0;
-  static Uint64 last_ns     = 0;
-  static bool   ft_inited   = false;
 
   // DOS-PORT (patch 0154, Phase 11 wave-58 -- FIXED_TIMESTEP steady-state
   // diagnostic; PHASE11-WAVE-58-CONTRACT.md sec.2). Per-100-frame block
diff --git a/src/map.cpp b/src/map.cpp
index 27ab106..187a6c1 100644
--- a/src/map.cpp
+++ b/src/map.cpp
@@ -23,6 +23,7 @@ using namespace NXE::Graphics;
 #include <fstream>
 #include <climits>
 #include <cstdlib>  // getenv
+#include <SDL3/SDL_dosaudio_pump.h>  // patch 0162: SDL_DOSAudioPump for the audio mid-gap pump
 
 stMap map;
 
@@ -958,18 +959,113 @@ uint32_t oob_tiles[4];
 
 // load stage "stage_no", this entails loading the map (pxm), enemies (pxe), tileset (pbm),
 // tile attributes (pxa), and script (tsc).
+// DOS-PORT (patch 0162-v2, Leg A audio mid-gap pump v2 -- the 486-class
+// SFX-stutter fix during stage loads, second iteration). v2 replaces
+// v1's once-per-seam pump with a pump-until-ring-full loop, adds the
+// FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator freeze/thaw around load_stage to prevent
+// TAS desync (the v1 iter's PLAY1 missed Shack because the pumps'
+// wall-clock cascaded into the catch-up tick_state count), and flips
+// the killswitch default from ON to OFF per flush-instr's safer-
+// landing recommendation. See docs/internal/AUDIO-MID-GAP-SERVICE
+// -DESIGN.md + 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.17.
+//
+// During a stage load the engine blocks in fread for tileset / map /
+// entities / script; the IRQ-5 ISR keeps draining the audio ring at
+// ~43 Hz throughout, and the cooperative audio thread cannot refill
+// while the main thread is blocked in disk I/O. A stage load longer
+// than the ring depth (~372 ms) underruns the ring -- the operator-
+// named ~1-second freeze with audio cutout. v2 calls SDL_DOSAudioPump()
+// in a `while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { }` loop between sub-loaders so
+// each seam tops up the ring to FULL (SDL_DOSAudioPump returns false
+// when there is no room for another chunk; v2 SDL/0067 export ABI).
+//
+// Killswitch: SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDGAP_PUMP. **v2 default OFF;
+// strict "1" enables.** The lever is opt-in until validated; team-lead
+// will flip back to default-ON in v3 if the v2 iter shows freeze
+// elimination + TAS sync both hold. Sentinel-cached (wave-54 PERF_MODE
+// / 0093 / 0153 / 0159 idiom) -- one SDL_GetHint on first call, cached
+// thereafter, NO per-pump getenv. First call emits the build-qa
+// BANNERS banner.
+//
+// FIXED_TIMESTEP freeze/thaw: ft_accumulator_freeze() (defined in
+// main.cpp) at load_stage entry records accum_ns; ft_accumulator_thaw()
+// at every load_stage exit (success or failure) restores accum_ns and
+// resets last_ns to SDL_GetTicksNS() -- so the wall-clock spent in
+// load_stage (including the pumps' time) is invisible to the
+// FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator's next delta. The exit-path coverage uses
+// the FtAccumulatorGuard RAII struct below, declared at load_stage
+// entry; its destructor fires on every return path. Both freeze and
+// thaw are gated on midgap_pump_active() -- when the killswitch is off
+// (the v2 default), neither fires and the FT=1 path matches v1.0.0 /
+// pre-Leg-A (matches the v1 iter's PLAY0-clean baseline per
+// 486-CLASS-CAMPAIGN-FINDINGS.md sec.17 asymmetry).
+//
+// SDL_DOSAudioPump is exported from sdl-engine's SDL/0067-v2 -- a thin
+// SDL_PlaybackAudioThreadIterate cycle with no SDL_PumpEvents, no
+// renderer-state touch, no engine-callback re-entry. load_stage runs
+// once per stage entry, not in any multi-run path, so the wave-36
+// drawcall-coupling trap does not apply here.
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_freeze(void);
+extern "C" void ft_accumulator_thaw(void);
+
+static int g_midgap_pump_decided = -1;
+static bool midgap_pump_active()
+{
+  if (g_midgap_pump_decided < 0)
+  {
+    const char *e = SDL_GetHint("SDL_HINT_DOSKUTSU_AUDIO_MIDGAP_PUMP");
+    g_midgap_pump_decided = (e && e[0] == '1' && e[1] == '\0') ? 1 : 0;
+    LOG_INFO("audio mid-gap pump: {}",
+             g_midgap_pump_decided ? "ENABLED (opt-in)" : "DISABLED (default)");
+  }
+  return g_midgap_pump_decided == 1;
+}
+#define MIDGAP_PUMP() do { if (midgap_pump_active()) while (SDL_DOSAudioPump()) { } } while (0)
+
+// RAII guard for the FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator across load_stage. The
+// constructor snapshots accum_ns at entry; the destructor restores it
+// and resets last_ns to NOW at every return path -- so wall-clock spent
+// in load_stage is invisible to the accumulator's next delta and the
+// catch-up loop does not amplify-then-desync the TAS replay. Both
+// freeze and thaw are gated on midgap_pump_active(): when the Leg A
+// killswitch is off (the v2 default), the guard is a no-op pair
+// (constructor + destructor each read the cached bool and return).
+struct FtAccumulatorGuard
+{
+  FtAccumulatorGuard()
+  {
+    if (midgap_pump_active())
+      ft_accumulator_freeze();
+  }
+  ~FtAccumulatorGuard()
+  {
+    if (midgap_pump_active())
+      ft_accumulator_thaw();
+  }
+};
+
 bool load_stage(int stage_no)
 {
   char fname[MAXPATHLEN];
+  // patch 0162-v2 FIX 2: snapshot/restore the FIXED_TIMESTEP accumulator
+  // across the entire stage load so the wall-clock spent here (including
+  // the Leg A audio pumps below) is invisible to the catch-up tick_state
+  // count. Destructor fires on every return path -- the 5 error
+  // early-returns and the success-path final return -- so the accumulator
+  // is never left frozen. Gated on midgap_pump_active() inside the
+  // ctor/dtor; killswitch off (v2 default) makes the guard a no-op pair.
+  FtAccumulatorGuard _ftg;
 
   LOG_INFO(" >> Entering stage {}: '{}'.", stage_no, stages[stage_no].stagename);
   game.curmap = stage_no; // do it now so onspawn events will have it
 
   Renderer::getInstance()->sprites.flushSheets();
   map_flush_graphics();
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 1: post-graphics-drop, pre-tileset.load
 
   if (!Renderer::getInstance()->tileset.load(stages[stage_no].tileset))
     return 1;
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 2: post-tileset.load (.pbm; the heavy sub-loader)
 
   // get the base name of the stage without extension
   const char *mapname = stages[stage_no].filename;
@@ -979,18 +1075,22 @@ bool load_stage(int stage_no)
   sprintf(fname, "Stage/%s.pxm", mapname);
   if (load_map(ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(fname, false)))
     return 1;
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 3: post-load_map (.pxm)
 
   sprintf(fname, "Stage/%s.pxa", tileset_names[stages[stage_no].tileset]);
   if (load_tileattr(ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(fname, false)))
     return 1;
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 4: post-load_tileattr (.pxa)
 
   sprintf(fname, "Stage/%s.pxe", mapname);
   if (load_entities(ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(fname, false)))
     return 1;
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 5: post-load_entities (.pxe)
 
   sprintf(fname, "Stage/%s.tsc", mapname);
   if (!game.tsc->Load(ResourceManager::getInstance()->getPath(fname), TSC::ScriptPages::SP_MAP))
     return 1;
+  MIDGAP_PUMP(); // patch 0162 Leg A seam 6: post-tsc->Load (.tsc)
   map_set_backdrop(stages[stage_no].bg_no);
   map.scrolltype = stages[stage_no].scroll_type;
   map.motionpos  = 0;
